{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794252794069,"sessionID":"ses_e3e3c21aeffe6lrXgrH6Q0fOV8","part":{"id":"prt_1c1cce8b90011Mslbd5Hy1QPdr","messageID":"msg_1c1ccb733001XKr4VOzDYwrD3l","sessionID":"ses_e3e3c21aeffe6lrXgrH6Q0fOV8","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794252794069,"sessionID":"ses_e3e3c21aeffe6lrXgrH6Q0fOV8","part":{"id":"prt_1c1cce8bb001qO2Gl6YzoBk9S9","messageID":"msg_1c1ccb733001XKr4VOzDYwrD3l","sessionID":"ses_e3e3c21aeffe6lrXgrH6Q0fOV8","type":"text","text":"I've built the kanban board: the Flask API with SQLite storage under `./data`, and the React + TypeScript + Tailwind frontend. I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't available here, and I couldn't test the web frontend in a browser because none is installed. That means drag and drop, the dialogs and sign-in were never tried by hand.\n\nWhat I did check: the frontend type-checks and `npm run build` succeeds. I ran the backend under gunicorn with the built frontend and exercised the API with scripts:\n- Register, login and the 401 without a token.\n- Validation errors.\n- Creating tasks at the end of a column.\n- Moving tasks within and between columns, and deleting them; positions stayed 1 to n with no gaps.\n- Filters and `counts`.\n- Not-found responses and the frontend being served at `/`.\n\nChoices I made that the spec didn't settle:\n- **Accounts:**\n  - Usernames are 3–32 characters (letters, digits, `_ . -`) and case-insensitive.\n  - Passwords need at least 6 characters.\n  - A taken username answers 409.\n  - Register also returns a token.\n  - Tokens don't expire; I added `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout`.\n- **Tasks:**\n  - Title is required (max 200 characters).\n  - Priority is `low`, `medium` or `high` and defaults to `medium`.\n  - New tasks go to `todo` unless a status is given.\n- **Errors:** validation failures answer 400 as `{\"error\": ..., \"errors\": {field: message}}`, and the dialogs show these messages next to each field.\n- **Out-of-range positions:** a `position` larger than the column is put at the end rather than rejected.\n- **Counts:** with the priority filter on, `counts` in the API reflects the filtered tasks. The board shows each column as \"filtered / total\".\n- **Refresh:** the board reloads every 15 seconds and when the window regains focus, so other users' changes show up.\n\n**Dependencies:** I added Tailwind 4.3.5, TypeScript and the React types to `frontend/package.json` and its lock file, plus `tsconfig.json`, an `npm run typecheck` script and a `.gitignore`. Python dependencies are unchanged. Most of the backend is in `backend/app.py`; the frontend is in `frontend/src/` (`App.tsx`, `api.ts`, `AuthForms.tsx`, `Dialogs.tsx`).","time":{"start":1794252794044,"end":1794252794047}}}
